WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.270
Everything you make here lives in your
browser, and it saves as you work.

2
00:00:04.362 --> 00:00:08.293
This episode is about what that
means, the one place it can bite,

3
00:00:08.293 --> 00:00:10.902
and how to keep a copy somewhere safer.

4
00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:17.211
Every open project is a tab: here's the
recipe book, and here's the 2026 planner.

5
00:00:17.257 --> 00:00:21.837
Each one keeps its own page, zoom
and undo history while you're away.

6
00:00:22.042 --> 00:00:25.262
The plus opens New
Project, from episode one.

7
00:00:25.292 --> 00:00:30.447
Each tab shows its project's name, and
renaming the top page in the tree renames the

8
00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:30.942
tab.

9
00:00:31.151 --> 00:00:35.531
Watch the badge beside the tabs while
I rename this to Family Cookbook.

10
00:00:35.625 --> 00:00:38.945
Saving locally while I
type, then Saved locally.

11
00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:40.809
There's nothing to press.

12
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.280
Every change is written into this
browser's own storage a moment later.

13
00:00:45.428 --> 00:00:48.078
Reload, and both tabs come straight back.

14
00:00:48.613 --> 00:00:50.742
Locally is the word to notice.

15
00:00:50.891 --> 00:00:53.421
It means this browser, on this computer.

16
00:00:53.497 --> 00:00:57.777
Clear the site's data, or switch
computers, and these tabs won't be there.

17
00:00:57.926 --> 00:01:00.036
Nor will any presets you've saved.

18
00:01:00.241 --> 00:01:04.241
Closing a tab is where work gets
lost, so the app asks first.

19
00:01:04.309 --> 00:01:06.739
Hover a tab, and its cross appears.

20
00:01:07.065 --> 00:01:10.980
As it says, closing removes the
whole project from this browser,

21
00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:13.615
and Close without Saving keeps no copy.

22
00:01:13.654 --> 00:01:17.354
This planner came straight from
a preset, so here that's fine.

23
00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:22.386
Anything you've worked on
deserves Save JSON & Close.

24
00:01:22.445 --> 00:01:26.345
It downloads the project as
one file, then closes the tab.

25
00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:30.100
Closing the last tab leaves
a blank project behind.

26
00:01:30.191 --> 00:01:35.201
And here's the file: plain text, holding
every page, template and variant.

27
00:01:35.302 --> 00:01:37.662
Keep it somewhere that isn't this browser.

28
00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:40.568
The app has no Open
button for these files.

29
00:01:40.652 --> 00:01:46.312
Instead, copy the whole file, and paste
it into the JSON editor, in a fresh tab.

30
00:01:46.516 --> 00:01:50.201
In Text mode, select all,
paste, and Apply Changes.

31
00:01:50.271 --> 00:01:54.451
The recipe book is back, and the
tab reads Family Cookbook again.

32
00:01:54.657 --> 00:01:58.577
Apply replaces whatever the
tab held, so use a blank one.

33
00:01:58.679 --> 00:02:02.419
Paste into the wrong tab, and
one Ctrl+Z takes it back.

34
00:02:02.624 --> 00:02:07.554
The other copy outside your browser
is a cloud save, from episode eleven.

35
00:02:07.632 --> 00:02:10.693
I'm signed in, so Cloud
offers Save to cloud (new):

36
00:02:10.693 --> 00:02:13.343
a version on the server, with a message.

37
00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:16.649
Closing a tab never
deletes those versions.

38
00:02:16.707 --> 00:02:21.481
The cookbook hasn't changed since I saved
it, so this time Close without Saving

39
00:02:21.481 --> 00:02:22.577
loses nothing.

40
00:02:22.782 --> 00:02:27.272
My projects, in the account menu, lists
everything you've saved to the cloud.

41
00:02:27.373 --> 00:02:30.353
Here's the cookbook:
private, with one version.

42
00:02:30.558 --> 00:02:35.858
Open loads its latest version into a new
tab, in any browser where you sign in.

43
00:02:35.914 --> 00:02:38.124
And here it is, back in the editor.

44
00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:42.462
It's still linked to its cloud
project: Cloud offers Save to cloud,

45
00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.500
not new, and Version history.

46
00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.950
The next save adds to the same history.

47
00:02:47.183 --> 00:02:51.576
So: let it save as you work, close
tabs with Save JSON & Close,

48
00:02:51.576 --> 00:02:53.918
and cloud-save the milestones.

49
00:02:54.031 --> 00:02:55.351
See you in the next one.
